    32	For `i` modulo 3, `i*i - i + 1` has residue 0 exactly when `i` has residue 2;
    33	otherwise it has residue 1. Therefore a three-element sum is divisible by 3
    34	exactly when the triple contains either zero or three residue-1 elements. There
    35	are `z = floor((N + 1) / 3)` residue-0 elements and `N - z` residue-1 elements,
    36	so the requested count is `C(z, 3) + C(N - z, 3)`. The proof-side definitions
    37	encode exactly that formula using the supplied semantics' Python-floor-division
    38	normal form.
