+
+PROOF BUILD COMMAND:
+kompile verification.k \
+  --backend haskell \
+  --main-module VERIFICATION \
+  --syntax-module VERIFICATION-SYNTAX \
+  --output-definition audit-verification-kompiled
+WORKDIR: /tmp/audit-work/147-clean-rebuild
+EXIT STATUS: 0
+RELEVANT OUTPUT:
+The compiler emitted only the four supplied strLt unused-variable warnings.
+
+POSITIVE CLAIM COMMAND:
+kprove spec.k \
+  --definition audit-verification-kompiled \
+  --spec-module SPEC
+WORKDIR: /tmp/audit-work/147-clean-rebuild
+EXIT STATUS: 0
+RELEVANT OUTPUT:
+Six non-fatal DecidePredicateUnknown diagnostics were emitted while builtin
+integer equations were being simplified/checked.
+#Top
+The compiler also repeated the four supplied strLt unused-variable warnings.
+
+CLAIM ACCOUNTING:
+spec.k contains exactly one positive claim, label SPEC.get-max-triples.
+It printed #Top and exited 0 in this clean reconstruction.

