+n=12 -> 60; n=13 -> 88; n=14 -> 94; n=15 -> 130; n=16 -> 175;
+n=17 -> 185; n=18 -> 240.
+LARGEST SAMPLED RESULT: n=120, canonical=92040, generated=92040.
+OUTSIDE CONTRACT: n=0 gives 0 in both implementations; n=-1 gives 0 in the
+canonical and -1 in the candidate. The latter divergence is excluded by the
+source contract and by the K claim's N >Int 0 precondition.
